    "text": "I read through the minbpe code this session: regex.py, basic.py, base.py, gpt4.py, __init__.py and the lineage_bench.py harness. I also searched for \"import\", which matched 60 lines, and for \"def _compile\\(\", which matched 0 lines, so the compile helper I expected is not there under that name.\n\nNothing measurable came out of it. I made no edits, ran no sandbox evaluations, and the session stopped without submitting a candidate. I have no numbers to report.\n\nWhat I believe now is limited to what reading gave me. The benchmark file is short and I have seen all of it. The tokenizer logic is spread across base.py, basic.py and regex.py. I have not tested any idea about where time goes, so any guess about the hot path is unverified.\n\nNext time I should stop reading and start measuring. I'll run lineage_bench.py on the unmodified code first to get a baseline. Then I'll pick one concrete change in the merge or encode loop of regex.py or basic.py, evaluate it in the sandbox, and submit only if it beats the baseline.",
